{
  "configuration_id": "config_042",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) achieved 0.650 acc, a large jump over config_011 (singleprofile, 0.520), showing multiprofile+avgpool is the dominant design lever. Meanwhile, adding image to the singleprofile setting (config_003, 0.532) barely helped over RNA alone (config_011, 0.520), and image alone was very weak (config_013, 0.227). Uncertainty: it is unclear whether image contributes any value on top of the much stronger multiprofile RNA baseline. This experiment (config_042: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) isolates the effect of adding the image modality by keeping the RNA encoder, profile setting, aggregation, and fusion strategy identical to the two best singleprofile comparisons (config_002 and config_003). If accuracy stays near 0.650, image adds little even in the multiprofile regime; if it improves meaningfully, it justifies further multimodal investment. This is the highest-information next step because it directly tests the most important open question—whether the image channel is worth the added complexity—while changing only one factor relative to the current best configuration."
}

